<urn:atm:triage:finding/AXPE-RBP-003>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AXPE-RBP-003" ;
  triage:title "escalate() takes a stringly-typed kind: &str instead of a closed enum" ;
  triage:description "crates/atm-http-runtime/src/herdr_escalation.rs escalate() function (line 147) takes escalation reason as kind: &str parameter with call sites passing raw string literals \"lead_notified\" (herdr_queue_wake.rs:2036, herdr_queue_wake_escalation.rs:67) and \"blocked_escalated\" (herdr_queue_wake_escalation.rs:225), unlike TaskState / TaskEventKind / ReminderOutcome enum pattern used elsewhere in Phase AX, losing exhaustiveness and rename safety. Remediation: introduce a closed EscalationKind enum with as_str() method for the tracing field, switch all call sites to use enum variants." ;
